  (assets/data/dushanbe.bin)


Source code — MIT OR Apache-2.0
-------------------------------

Unless a file says otherwise, the source code is dual-licensed under the MIT License
(LICENSE-MIT) and the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE); you may use it under
either. This is the usual arrangement in the Rust ecosystem: MIT is short and permissive,
Apache-2.0 adds an explicit patent grant.

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for inclusion in this
repository, as defined in the Apache-2.0 licence, is dual-licensed as above, without any
additional terms or conditions.


The Lab articles — CC BY 4.0
----------------------------

The articles in content/*/lab/ may be shared and adapted for any purpose, including
commercially, if you credit "Mintaka" with a link to the original article and indicate any
changes you made. The code they quote is part of the source code above.
Full terms: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode


Brand, copy and portraits — all rights reserved
-----------------------------------------------

The Mintaka name, logo and star mark identify our company; please don't use them for your own
products or in a way that suggests we endorse you. The site's copy is ours. The portraits show
real people, published with their consent for this site only; they are not licensed for any
other use. If you fork the code, replace all three with your own.


Third-party material
--------------------

- Space Grotesk, Onest and IBM Plex Mono are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the
  licence texts are in assets/fonts/licenses/.
- assets/data/dushanbe.bin is a database derived from OpenStreetMap data,
  © OpenStreetMap contributors, and is available under the Open Database License 1.0
  (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/). The site shows the attribution next to the
  map; assets/data/README.md describes how the file is produced.
- Time zone locations come from the IANA time zone database, which is in the public domain.

Dependencies fetched by Cargo and npm come with their own licences.
